    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Description\n\nRecently, moving away from many plugins, one of which is [`which-key`](https://github.com/folke/which-key.nvim). Migrating away I find myself missing the feature where `which-key` would popup spelling suggestions.\n\nWould it be possible to configure `mini.clue` to do something like this? I did see that there is:\n```lua\nclues = {\n      { mode = 'i', keys = '<C-x><C-s>', desc = 'Spelling suggestions' },\n}\n```\nBut I am interested in the normal mode `z=`\n\nThank you for the awesome plugins :)",
