        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "So I've taken a look and this looks like the best approach that can be done with 'mini.clue':\n\n```lua\nlocal make_spellsuggest_clues = function(labels)\n  labels = labels or '123456789abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz'\n  local labels_arr, n = vim.split(labels, ''), labels:len()\n\n  return function()\n    -- Get suggestions for word under cursor\n    local word = vim.fn.expand('<cword>')\n    local suggestions = vim.fn.spellsuggest(word, n)\n\n    -- Construct clues for each combination of `z=`+label that will emulate\n    -- the following keys: `z=` + <label> + <C-u> (clear) + <index> + <CR>\n    -- This takes advantage of:\n    -- - Built-in `z=` waits for the whole index to be confirmed with <CR>.\n    -- - Allows typing any letter before pressing <CR>.\n    -- - Allows <C-u> to remove all text to the left of cursor.\n    local res = {}\n    for i = 1, n do\n      local label, desc = labels_arr[i], suggestions[i]\n      local postkeys = '<C-u>' .. i .. '<CR>'\n      table.insert(res, { mode = 'n', keys = 'z=' .. label, desc = desc, postkeys = postkeys })\n    end\n    return res\n  end\nend\n\nlocal miniclue = require('mini.clue')\nminiclue.setup({\n  clues = {\n    -- Create a function that will be run on every clue window initialization\n    make_spellsuggest_clues(),\n    -- ... Other clues\n  },\n  triggers = {\n    { mode = 'n', keys = 'z' }, -- `z` key\n    -- ... Other triggers\n  },\n})\n```\n\nMost of the details are in code comments. Unfortunately, I believe this is a rather hacky solution:\n- As 'mini.clue' always emulates typed keys as is, it results into opening the built-in window that waits for the user to input a number and confirm with `<CR>`. With the above solution this might result in a small flicker.\n- As 'mini.clue' only allows `postkeys` to be string and not arbitrary action function (not entirely sure why, probably to limit already high complexity without obvious benefits), the above solution has to go the hacky route of `<C-u>`.\n\nSo I am going to close this as both \"already possible\" and \"I'd still recommend to use custom mapping for more comfortable spell suggestions\".",
